## Feature #2 Increment 3b (spec §4.2) — SUPERVISED scope (the named
## exception, `s.collect_supervised`). Children fail INDEPENDENTLY: all run
## to completion regardless of errors, no sibling cancellation; collect
## returns the COUNT of children that errored. Mirrors Kotlin's
## `supervisorScope` / Java's `Joiner`.
##
## Three children all COMPLETE: ok (1), fail (-1), ok2 (2). Unlike fail-fast,
## the error does NOT cancel siblings — every child runs (all three "ran"
## lines print), and collect returns 1 (one errored).

async def ok1() -> Int
  puts "ok1 ran"
  1
end

async def failing() -> Int
  puts "failing ran"
  0 - 1
end

async def ok2() -> Int
  puts "ok2 ran"
  2
end

def main
  puts "scope start"
  Scope.open do |s|
    s.spawn(ok1())
    s.spawn(failing())
    s.spawn(ok2())
    let errors = s.collect_supervised
    puts "errors=#{errors}"
  end
  puts "scope done"
end
